{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/build.gradle.kts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:59:20.631657Z","id":"2186b3fd0b0ba5058b3c442986cdbbe46d3f0a8c7cd7cc7c299f95ecb3246e6f","body":{"detail":"`flutter config --list` shows no jdk-dir, and no system Java is installed. `flutter build apk --debug` failed at Gradle's start with \"Unable to locate a Java Runtime\"; with JAVA_HOME=~/Library/Java/jdk-17.0.20.1+1/Contents/Home (and its bin on PATH) the same build succeeded and produced app-debug.apk (minSdk 29, INTERNET, RECORD_AUDIO, extractNativeLibs, lib/arm64-v8a/libclax.so). Recipes that build the APK must set JAVA_HOME, or the machine's Flutter needs `flutter config --jdk-dir <JDK 17 home>`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"bb0eaab029d7f95418f63f2192a8080610903cf560fd0ee143868652be0f3e1b"},"suggested_fix":"Set JAVA_HOME to the JDK 17 home in the APK build recipes (scripts/build-app-clax.sh, justfile app-apk), or configure flutter's jdk-dir once on the machine.","summary":"Flutter has no JDK configured: `flutter build apk` fails with \"Unable to locate a Java Runtime\" unless JAVA_HOME names JDK 17","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/build.gradle.kts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:59:20.631754Z","id":"a4af31346481214115ef9d260171a0729e685a58e59f1124e9c310daef67b7a8","body":{"detail":"`flutter build apk --debug` produced lib/armeabi-v7a/libflutter.so beside arm64-v8a and x86_64 although defaultConfig.ndk.abiFilters lists only arm64-v8a and x86_64 (aapt dump badging: native-code 'arm64-v8a' 'armeabi-v7a' 'x86_64'). No libclax.so exists for armeabi-v7a, so the app installed on a 32-bit-only device would start without its daemon. A release build should pass --target-platform android-arm64,android-x64.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"880e8e2ada826b606eb231851e6b092f8b9b1a8edcf9102afe97f0f81ee57b77"},"suggested_fix":"Build release APKs with `--target-platform android-arm64,android-x64`.","summary":"A debug APK still carries armeabi-v7a: the Flutter Gradle plugin adds its own ABIs to abiFilters","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/build.gradle.kts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:04:07.305115Z","id":"70f187c547877458505612748037e860b27f3ac843b45bb4ac4fe98eadaf9c41","body":{"detail":"`flutter config --list` shows `jdk-dir: /Users/alex/Library/Java/jdk-17.0.20.1+1/Contents/Home`; `flutter doctor -v` reports that JDK as \"specified in your Flutter configuration\". With no system JDK (`/usr/libexec/java_home` answers \"Unable to locate a Java Runtime\"), `env -u JAVA_HOME flutter build apk --debug` in apps/clax_app printed `✓ Built build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk` and exited 0. The fix is machine configuration, not repository content: another machine needs the same `flutter config --jdk-dir`.","kind":"comment","references":"2186b3fd0b0ba5058b3c442986cdbbe46d3f0a8c7cd7cc7c299f95ecb3246e6f","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"bb0eaab029d7f95418f63f2192a8080610903cf560fd0ee143868652be0f3e1b"},"summary":"Flutter now has a JDK configured, and `flutter build apk --debug` succeeds without JAVA_HOME","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
